% ============================================================================
% quadrilateral-types.query.adj — a worked recall over the geometry
% quadrilateral-types library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what makes a rhombus a
% rhombus?": it states no geometry fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against
% the `quadrilateral_property` rows and returns the property + the table's
% source/locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the
% property `four_right_angles`, recall its quadrilateral — rectangle). A word
% that is not one of the five named quadrilaterals abstains honestly — the
% engine never invents a property.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli quadrilateral-types.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "quadrilateral-types.adj"

? quadrilateral_property(rhombus, $Property)         % expect all_sides_same_length
? quadrilateral_property(parallelogram, $Property)   % expect opposite_sides_parallel
? quadrilateral_property(trapezoid, $Property)       % expect two_sides_parallel
? quadrilateral_property($Shape, four_right_angles)  % reverse bind — expect rectangle
? quadrilateral_property(triangle, $Property)        % expect abstain — a triangle has three sides, not a quadrilateral
